# AI-Powered Recommendations (Minimal Impact)

## Goal
- Add personalized recommendations without changing core trip search, booking, cancellation, or external integration workflows.
- Keep AI as a ranking/enrichment layer, not a source of truth.

## Implementation Scope (Minimal)
- Add backend endpoint: `GET /api/recommendations`.
- Keep existing endpoints (`/api/trips`, `/api/bookings`, `/api/notifications`) unchanged.
- On frontend, only replace/augment home recommendations fetch logic; keep current UI components.
- Add a dedicated system prompt file for Gemini constraints/rules (for example: `backend/app/services/prompts/recommendation_system_prompt.txt`).

## Data and Prompt Rules
- Build candidate trips server-side first (availability, dates, basic filters).
- Send Gemini only minimal user context and candidate summaries (no sensitive PII).
- Require strict JSON output: ranked `trip_id` list, optional `score`, optional short `reason`.
- Load a fixed system prompt from the dedicated prompt file and combine it with request-specific user/candidate context.

## Safety and Reliability
- Validate Gemini output agaainst candidate set (valid ids, no duplicates, bounded result count).
- Enforce timeout and catch parse/model errors.
- If AI fails, fallback to deterministic ranking (current rule-based logic).
- Never block booking flow due to recommendation service errors.
- Keep system prompt instructions deterministic: ranking-only behavior, no policy overrides, no unsupported fields in output.

## Workflow Compatibility
- Recommendations are additive and read-only.
- Booking source branching (local vs external) remains unchanged.
- Notifications, favorites rules, and external adapter contracts remain unchanged.

## Configuration
- Store `GEMINI_API_KEY` only in backend enviaronment.
- Never expose provider keys to frontend.
- Add model/timeout config with safe defaults.
- Version and own the system prompt file in repo so recommendation behavior is auditable and reproducible.

## Done Criteria
- Home page shows AI-ranked trips when available.
- Automatic fallback returns deterministic recommendations when AI is unavailable.
- Existing search, booking, cancel, and notification flows pass unchanged.
